# GTM price lists: bump revision date on every content change

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-09-22):

> **yes, always on any change** — bump the price-list header
> revision date, and make it standing practice that **every**
> price-list content change updates that date.

## The rule

> **When any customer-facing price list markdown, canvas, or kit
> content changes, bump `PRICE_LIST_PUBLICATION_DATE` in
> `operator-workflows/scripts/contracts/render-contract.py` (and
> every matching canvas / inline date line) to the change date
> (YYYY-MM-DD) in the **same** change set, then re-render Word and
> Portable Document Format (PDF). Never leave Word or PDF on a
> stale header date while body content changed.**

## Surfaces that must match

| Surface | What to bump |
| --- | --- |
| Renderer | `PRICE_LIST_PUBLICATION_DATE` (keeps the `\| Prices are subject to change without notice.` suffix via `PRICE_LIST_NOTICE`) |
| Enterprise markdown / canvas | Header-style date line; `source: Rebuilt …` when present |
| Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification (CMMC) solutions canvas | Parallel date line when present |
| Secure Enclave | Renderer header (no separate inline date unless one is added) |
| Azure CMMC hosted card | Paper "last edited" / canvas source date when that line is the card's stamp |

## Required sequence

1. Set the date to the session / change date (not yesterday's stamp).
2. Sync every parallel customer-facing date line in the same edit.
3. Re-render Enterprise, CMMC Solutions, and Secure Enclave (and
   Azure Word/PDF if those exist). Refresh family-folder and kit
   copies per
   [`gtm-contracts-render-commit-push.mdc`](gtm-contracts-render-commit-push.mdc).
4. Commit and push explicit paths in `pam-platform-docs` and
   `operator-workflows` (and `core-assets` when this rule changes).

## Forbidden

- Changing price-list body / SKU / note content without bumping the
  date in the same change set
- Shipping Word or PDF whose second header line still shows an older
  date than the markdown or canvas just edited
- Inventing prices or Met / certified claims while touching dates
- Leaving only one of renderer / canvas / markdown on the new date

